# tests/merge, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs. Pure
# evaluation, so a broken expression is told apart from a failing assertion and
# the request has a name before it is dispatched.
#
# A CLIENT TEST — it drives `caos-cli`, so its base is `DEEP-DEPS/cli-test`
# (dev/cli-test), the image that stages a git worktree and then runs `worker1`.
# DEPping on `lib` is the greppable marker of which tests are client tests.
#
#   --test  this directory itself, staged into the repo as ./test with its
#           DEEP-DEPS alongside. `--test:@=.` is inert by construction:
#           `strip_caos_expr` removes this file from the tree before the
#           expression is evaluated against it, so nothing recurses.
#
# NOTHING HERE NAMES WHAT ONLY THE RUN KNOWS. The client under test, the salt,
# and a workspace or api key are PASSED when dev/run-test calls this ArgTree —
# so every path above exists in this directory, which is the whole point of an
# expression being readable on its own.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/cli-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --test:@=.
